[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-overview-1600x120.png[/img]
Venworks Customizable HUD provides five separately packaged Starfield HUD themes rendered through Venworks Canvas. The themes use HTML, CSS, and SVG presentation while retaining their own plugins, status-effect catalogs, and tactical display behavior.

[size=3][b][u]Requirements[/u][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/7097]Venworks - Core Utilities[/url] version 2.1.8 or newer.[/*]
[*]Install Venworks Canvas version 1.0.4 or newer.[/*]
[*]Install exactly one VWHUD theme.[/*]
[/list]

The Canvas Example is not required. Do not install an earlier standalone VWHUD HUD replacement alongside a Canvas consumer package.

[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-features-1600x120.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Compass heading, threat state, and compact paged status effects.[/*]
[*]Player health, oxygen, CO2, boost, carry mass, currency, time, and progression information.[/*]
[*]Equipment, weapon, ammunition, explosive, and power information in the four full themes.[/*]
[*]Environment panels for location, time, gravity, suit protection, and active hazards.[/*]
[*]Tracked objective, acquired-contact radar, and forward scanner presentation.[/*]
[*]Bethesda's current vehicle-exit glyph through Canvas's native symbol adapter.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][u]Themes[/u][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Venworks[/*]
[*]Trackers Alliance[/*]
[*]Freestar Collective[/*]
[*]Crimson Fleet[/*]
[*]Minimalist[/*]
[/list]

Minimalist uses a reduced holographic composition without the faction crest or equipment rail. Enable only one theme at a time.

[size=3][b][u]Packages[/u][/b][/size]

Nexus PC - Normal contains the theme's real ESM and Windows Main BA2. Nexus PC - Fully Loose Files contains the same plugin, compiled scripts, and complete consumer Interface tree for inspection or controlled customization. Do not install both package shapes together.

Theme assets are stored under Canvas's isolated consumer directory. They remain VWHUD-owned files; the theme packages do not copy Canvas framework code or host movies.

[size=3][b][u]Customization on PC[/u][/b][/size]

Every theme loads a VWHUD-owned [b]vwhud-overrides.css[/b] file after its base layout and palette. With the Normal package, install your override as a separate mod after VWHUD to change colors, placement, size, typography, or panel visibility while keeping the VWHUD package archive-only. Use the Fully Loose Files package for complete HTML, CSS, and SVG changes.

The [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui/blob/master/docs/CUSTOMIZING_THEMES.md]VWHUD customization guide[/url] lists the exact theme paths, stable panel classes, examples, update procedure, and reset procedure. Canvas defines the supported HTML, CSS, SVG, and component syntax.

[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-known-issues-1600x120.png[/img]
[list]
[*]This release remains beta until exact-package PC and console acceptance is complete.[/*]
[*]The radar displays contacts already supplied by Starfield; it is not a life-form detector.[/*]
[*]Large-HUD, ultrawide, sustained-update, and console feedback remain valuable.[/*]
[*]Compatibility with HUD replacements is governed by Venworks Canvas because Canvas owns the shared host movies.[/*]
[/list]

[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-source-code-1600x120.png[/img]
Source, user documentation, build documentation, and validation boundaries are available at [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui]GitHub[/url].
